# Astro Excellence

## Component Syntax

Astro components use a two-section format: a fenced code block (Component Script) followed by a template (Component Template). Unlike JSX, the template is HTML-first.

```astro
---
// Component Script — runs at build time (or server-side in SSR mode)
// Import components, fetch data, define props here
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Card from '../components/Card.astro'

interface Props {
  title: string
  description?: string
}

const { title, description = '' } = Astro.props

const posts = await Astro.glob('../content/blog/*.md')
---

<!-- Component Template — plain HTML + Astro expressions -->
<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  {description && <p class="lead">{description}</p>}

  <ul>
    {posts.map((post) => (
      <li>
        <Card title={post.frontmatter.title} href={post.url} />
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
```

- The Component Script is **server-only** — no browser APIs unless inside a `<script>` tag
- Expressions use single curly braces `{value}`, not JSX double-brace
- Use `{condition && <Element />}` or ternary for conditional rendering; no `if` blocks in templates
- `class` is the attribute name (not `className`); `class:list` accepts arrays and objects for conditional classes

## Islands Architecture (Client Directives)

By default every component renders to static HTML. Add a **client directive** to hydrate a component in the browser.

```astro
---
import Counter from '../components/Counter.jsx'
import HeavyChart from '../components/HeavyChart.vue'
import SearchBox from '../components/SearchBox.svelte'
---

<!-- Hydrate immediately — use sparingly, only for above-the-fold critical UI -->
<Counter client:load />

<!-- Hydrate when the component enters the viewport (lazy) -->
<HeavyChart client:visible />

<!-- Hydrate after page load, during browser idle time -->
<SearchBox client:idle />

<!-- Hydrate only on a media query match -->
<MobileMenu client:media="(max-width: 768px)" />

<!-- Hydrate only when a parent component passes the 'client:only' hint (skips SSR entirely) -->
<MapWidget client:only="react" />
```

- Omit the directive → zero JS shipped, pure HTML
- `client:load` is the most expensive; default to `client:visible` or `client:idle`
- `client:only` skips server rendering — use when the component relies on browser-only APIs (e.g., `window`, `localStorage`)

## File-Based Routing

```
src/pages/
├── index.astro           # Renders at /
├── about.astro           # Renders at /about
├── blog/
│   ├── index.astro       # Renders at /blog
│   └── [slug].astro      # Renders at /blog/:slug (static: getStaticPaths required)
├── [...path].astro       # Catch-all: /anything/nested
└── api/
    └── search.ts         # API endpoint — export GET, POST, etc.
```

### Dynamic Routes with `getStaticPaths`

```astro
---
// src/pages/blog/[slug].astro
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await getCollection('blog')
  return posts.map((post) => ({
    params: { slug: post.slug },
    props: { post },
  }))
}

const { post } = Astro.props
const { Content } = await post.render()
---

<article>
  <h1>{post.data.title}</h1>
  <Content />
</article>
```

- `getStaticPaths` must export from every `[dynamic]` page in static output mode
- Return `{ params, props }` — `props` are available as `Astro.props` in the component
- For SSR mode (`output: 'server'`), `getStaticPaths` is not used; read `Astro.params` directly

## Content Collections

Content Collections are the recommended way to manage structured content (blog posts, docs, authors).

```typescript
// src/content/config.ts
import { defineCollection, z } from 'astro:content'

const blog = defineCollection({
  type: 'content',  // 'content' for .md/.mdx, 'data' for .yaml/.json
  schema: z.object({
    title: z.string(),
    description: z.string(),
    pubDate: z.coerce.date(),
    tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
    draft: z.boolean().default(false),
    heroImage: z.string().optional(),
  }),
})

const authors = defineCollection({
  type: 'data',
  schema: z.object({
    name: z.string(),
    bio: z.string(),
    avatar: z.string(),
  }),
})

export const collections = { blog, authors }
```

```astro
---
// Querying collections
import { getCollection, getEntry } from 'astro:content'

// Get all published posts, newest first
const posts = (await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf())

// Get a single entry by collection + slug
const author = await getEntry('authors', 'jane-doe')
---
```

- Always define schemas in `src/content/config.ts` — Astro infers TypeScript types from the Zod schema
- Use `type: 'content'` for Markdown/MDX, `type: 'data'` for JSON/YAML reference data
- Filter collections at query time (`getCollection(name, filter)`) rather than filtering the array after

## API Endpoints

```typescript
// src/pages/api/posts.ts
import type { APIRoute } from 'astro'
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'

export const GET: APIRoute = async ({ url }) => {
  const tag = url.searchParams.get('tag')
  const posts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) =>
    !data.draft && (!tag || data.tags.includes(tag))
  )

  return new Response(
    JSON.stringify(posts.map((p) => ({ slug: p.slug, ...p.data }))),
    { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } }
  )
}

export const POST: APIRoute = async ({ request }) => {
  const body = await request.json()
  // handle mutation...
  return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }), { status: 201 })
}
```

- Export named functions (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`) for each HTTP method
- Return a `Response` object — use `new Response(body, { status, headers })` or Astro's `redirect()`
- API endpoints work in both static (`output: 'static'`, pre-rendered) and SSR mode

## Layouts

```astro
---
// src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro
import '../styles/global.css'

interface Props {
  title: string
  description?: string
}

const { title, description = 'My Astro site' } = Astro.props
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <nav>...</nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <slot />              <!-- Default slot: page content goes here -->
    </main>
    <footer>
      <slot name="footer" /> <!-- Named slot -->
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
```

```astro
---
// Using a named slot from a page
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <p>Main content goes into the default slot.</p>
  <p slot="footer">This goes into the named footer slot.</p>
</BaseLayout>
```

## View Transitions

```astro
---
// src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro
import { ViewTransitions } from 'astro:transitions'
---

<head>
  <ViewTransitions />
</head>
```

```astro
<!-- Opt individual elements out of the default morph animation -->
<aside transition:name="sidebar" transition:animate="slide">...</aside>

<!-- Persist an element across navigations (e.g. an audio player) -->
<audio transition:persist src="/music.mp3" />
```

- Add `<ViewTransitions />` once in your base layout to enable SPA-like navigation
- `transition:name` links the "same" element across pages for a smooth morph animation — names must be unique per page
- `transition:persist` keeps the element mounted without re-rendering during navigation

## astro.config.mjs

```javascript
// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config'
import react from '@astrojs/react'
import tailwind from '@astrojs/tailwind'
import mdx from '@astrojs/mdx'
import sitemap from '@astrojs/sitemap'

export default defineConfig({
  site: 'https://example.com',
  output: 'static',           // 'static' | 'server' | 'hybrid'
  integrations: [
    react(),
    tailwind(),
    mdx(),
    sitemap(),
  ],
  markdown: {
    shikiConfig: {
      theme: 'github-dark',
    },
  },
})
```

- `output: 'static'` (default) — fully pre-rendered at build time
- `output: 'server'` — fully server-rendered (requires an adapter: `@astrojs/node`, `@astrojs/cloudflare`, etc.)
- `output: 'hybrid'` — static by default, opt specific pages into SSR with `export const prerender = false`

## Key Rules

- Component Script runs **once at build/request time** — never use `document`, `window`, or event listeners there; put those in `<script>` tags or client-framework components
- Pass data from the server to a `<script>` tag via `define:vars={{ myVar }}` directive
- Prefer `Astro.glob()` for local file imports; use `getCollection()` for typed content collections
- In SSR mode, `Astro.cookies`, `Astro.request`, and `Astro.redirect()` are available for server-side logic
- MDX files can import and use Astro/React/Vue/Svelte components — use `.mdx` extension and the `@astrojs/mdx` integration
- `class:list={[...]}` is the Astro equivalent of `clsx`/`classnames` for conditional CSS classes
